  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-text"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
      <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text-text paragraph--view-mode--default">
      <div class="text-text">
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><h2>How you benefit from our programmes</h2>
<p>As an Aalto student, you'll enjoy the benefits offered by the programmes and Aalto University:</p>
<ul>
<li>Innovative, future-oriented programmes.</li>
<li>Aalto's unique combination of fields - combine business, art and technology in your studies!</li>
<li>State-of-the-art faculty. Teaching based on top-notch research and real-world applications.</li>
<li>International career opportunities and degrees valued by employers.</li>
<li>Tight industry relations and a thriving startup ecosystem.</li>
<li>Main campus in the vibrant Helsinki capital region.</li>
<li>Inspiring international Aalto community.</li>
</ul>
<h2><br>From bachelor's to master's</h2>
<p>In our bachelor's programmes, you'll get an automatic study right to a master's programme. After graduating from the bachelor's&nbsp;programme, you will automatically have&nbsp;the right to continue studies in selected master's programmes.</p>
<p>Aalto University has about 100 different master's programmes. You can find Aalto University's entire programme offering on the <a href="/en/node/32226">Study options</a> website.</p>
<p>Information on Aalto bachelor's programmes in Finnish and Swedish is available on the website <a href="/fi/node/54501">Hae suomen- ja ruotsinkielisiin kandidaattikoulutuksiin</a> (only in Finnish/Swedish).</p></div>
            </div>
    </div>
  
      </div>

      

  <div class=" aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-highlight"
        lang="en"       style="">
        <div class="text-highlight text-highlight--theme4">
      <aside>
        <p>At Aalto University, you&#039;ll get to study in an international and multidisciplinary environment together with students from all around the globe! </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
        </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-text"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
      <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text-text paragraph--view-mode--default">
      <div class="text-text">
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><h2>Programmes</h2>
<p>At Aalto University, we offer six English-taught bachelor’s programmes. Below you can find links to the programme descriptions.</p>
<p><strong>Programmes / majors</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field of Art and design</strong><br><a href="/en/node/54651/">Design and Media</a></p>
<p><strong>Field of Business and economics</strong></p>
<p><a href="/en/node/31971/">Economics</a></p>
<p><a href="/en/node/15521/">International Business</a></p>
<p><a href="/en/node/1379707">Finance</a></p>
<p><strong>Field of Science and technology</strong></p>
<p>Bachelor's Programme in Science and Technology, majors/study options:</p>
<p><a href="/en/node/31816/">Chemical Engineering</a></p>
<p><a href="/en/node/1173346/">Computer Engineering</a></p>
<p><a href="/en/node/31156">Data Science</a></p>
<p><a href="/en/node/30601/">Digital Systems and Design</a></p>
<p><a href="/en/node/31796">Mechanical and Civil Engineering</a></p>
<p><a href="/en/node/32421/">Quantum Technology</a></p>
<p><strong>Interdisciplinary programme</strong></p>
<p><a href="/en/node/1376781">Bachelor’s programme in Technology, Business and Design</a></p></div>
            </div>
    </div>
  
      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-accordion"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
  <div class="paragraph--text-accordion component-container">
      <div class="accordion__container">
                        <div class="listing-accordion__container">  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content"
          id="accordion-title"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Are you already a student at Aalto University or an Aalto University graduate?
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title" id="accordion-content">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>As an Aalto University student, you cannot be granted a right to pursue a degree in a study option if you have already earned a degree or have a valid right to pursue one in that study option.&nbsp;</p>
<p>If you have a valid right to study only for a Master of Science (Economics and Business Administration) at the Aalto University School of Business, you cannot be admitted to the undergraduate level study options in the field of business and economics at Aalto University.</p></div>
            
  </div>

  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--2"
          id="accordion-title--2"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    One study right rule
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--2" id="accordion-content--2">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>If you have a study right at a Finnish higher education institution, please note the amendment to the Universities Act and the new one study right rule.</p>
<p>Under the amended Universities Act (42 a §), your study rights at the same or lower level will be terminated if you accept a new study right leading to a degree.</p>
<p>Previous study rights remain valid until the new study right begins and are terminated on the preceding day. The study right granted in Aalto University’s bachelor's admissions begins on 1 August.</p>
<p>This rule applies only to study rights at higher education institutions in Finland.</p>
<p>Read more about the <a href="https://opintopolku.fi/konfo/en/sivu/the-one-study-right-rule">one study right rule on Studyinfo</a> (studyinfo.fi).&nbsp;</p></div>
            
  </div>

</div>
      </div>
  </div>

      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-text"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
      <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text-text paragraph--view-mode--default">
      <div class="text-text">
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><h2>When to apply?</h2>
<p>You apply either in Admission round A or Admission round B. The application period for both rounds is from 7 to 22 January 2027. Read the section <em>Application process</em> on this page to find which admission round is correct for you.</p></div>
            </div>
    </div>
  
      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-text"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
      <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text-text paragraph--view-mode--default">
      <div class="text-text">
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><h2><strong>Who can apply?</strong></h2>
<p>All applicants must fulfill the general eligibility requirements for higher education and submit the required documents by the given deadlines.&nbsp;</p>
<p>You are eligible to apply if you have completed or will complete during spring 2027 one of the following qualifications:</p>
<ul>
<li>Finnish matriculation examination</li>
<li>International Baccalaureate (IB) diploma, completed in an accredited IB&nbsp;school</li>
<li>European Baccalaureate (EB) diploma,&nbsp;completed in an accredited EB school</li>
<li>Deutsches Internationales Abitur diploma (DIA) or&nbsp;Reifeprüfung diploma (RP), completed in Finland</li>
<li>Upper secondary education completed outside Finland, for example a high school diploma. The qualification must&nbsp;give eligibility to the corresponding level of higher education in the country in which it was awarded.</li>
<li>A Finnish vocational upper secondary qualification, further vocational qualification or specialist vocational qualification as set in the Vocational Education Act (531/2017)</li>
<li>Advanced International Certificate of Education diploma (AICE)</li>
</ul>
<p>Additionally eligible to apply are</p>
<ul>
<li>applicants who have been granted the right to study in a university in Finland</li>
<li>applicants who have a higher education degree completed in Finland</li>
<li>applicants who have at minimum a bachelor level degree completed outside Finland</li>
</ul></div>
            </div>
    </div>
  
      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-accordion"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
  <div class="paragraph--text-accordion component-container">
      <div class="accordion__container">
                  <h2>  Application process
</h2>
                          <div class="listing-accordion__description">  <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>You apply either in <a href="/en/node/1389254">Admission round A or Admission round B</a>. The application period for both rounds is from 7 to 22 January 2027, but the admission results are published at different times. The correct admission round depends on the study option (or options) you are applying to and your educational background. Check the information below to find the correct application round.</p></div>
</div>
                <div class="listing-accordion__container">  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--3"
          id="accordion-title--3"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Applying to the Bachelor’s programme in Design and Media
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--3" id="accordion-content--3">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>The only scenario in which you can apply in both application rounds is if you are applying to the fields of science and technology or business and economics on the basis of SAT or ACT test results as well as to the Design and Media programme, and your eligibility is based on a qualification other than the Finnish matriculation examination, International Baccalaureate (IB), European Baccalaureate (EB), or a Finnish Reifeprüfung (RP) or Deutsche Internationale Abitur (DIA).&nbsp;In this case, you must submit a separate application form and required application documents for each round. Design and Media has <a href="/en/node/54586">its own instructions page</a>.</p></div>
            
  </div>

</div>
      </div>
  </div>

      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-text"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
      <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text-text paragraph--view-mode--default">
      <div class="text-text">
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>You can apply to a maximum of three study options within one admission round. You may only be admitted to one study option. View all study options available at Aalto University on the page&nbsp;<a href="/en/node/32226">Study options</a>.</p>
<p>Read the application instructions and document requirements carefully. You can edit your application form during the application period. Upload all the required application documents to your application form by the given deadlines.</p>
<p>If you want to apply in any other application rounds as well, you must separately complete the correct application form during the application period and submit any required attachments by the given deadlines. If you apply in multiple application rounds, submitting the attachments for one application is not sufficient; you must submit them separately for each application round.</p></div>
            </div>
    </div>
  
      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--image-single"
        lang="en"       style="">
         
<div class="single-image single-image--medium">
    


<figure>
  <div class=" single-image__image-wrapper">
    <div class="media-with-caption__container single-image__image-container">
      
                    


  
      
                      <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/o_914w_ah_n_nu/public/2026-10/EN_aalto_bachelors_admissions_1.10.2026.jpg?itok=_a_Ujfkb" width="914" height="641" alt="A table showing 2027 bachelor’s admission rounds A and B at Aalto University with dates." />



            
  

            
    </div>
  </div>
  </figure>
</div>
      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-accordion"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
  <div class="paragraph--text-accordion component-container">
      <div class="accordion__container">
                  <h2>  Admission round A
</h2>
                          <div class="listing-accordion__description">  <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>You can apply to the following bachelor's programmes in admission round A:</p>
<ul>
<li>Bachelor’s Programme in Technology, Business, and Design</li>
<li>Bachelor’s Programme in Economics</li>
<li>Bachelor’s Programme in Finance</li>
<li>Bachelor's Programme in International Business</li>
</ul>

<p>Bachelor's Programme in Science and Technology, study options:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Chemical Engineering</li>
<li>Computer Engineering</li>
<li>Data Science</li>
<li>Digital Systems and Design</li>
<li>Mechanical and Civil Engineering</li>
<li>Quantum Technology</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Eligibility in admission round A:</strong> applicants who fulfill the general eligibility requirements for higher education, but have not completed or will not complete in spring 2027&nbsp;the Finnish Matriculation Examination, the&nbsp;International Baccalaureate (IB), the&nbsp;European Baccalaureate&nbsp;(EB), the&nbsp;Deutsches Internationales Abitur (DIA) or Reifeprüfung (RP) diploma (DIA/RP diploma completed in Finland only). For example, if you are completing a high school diploma in Vietnam or the A-levels, you apply in this admission round.</p>
<p><strong>Admission result publication: </strong>The admission results for admission round A are published by March 2027.</p></div>
</div>
                <div class="listing-accordion__container">  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--4"
          id="accordion-title--4"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Admission method in admission round A
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--4" id="accordion-content--4">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>SAT or ACT test results. On the Bachelor's programme in Technology, Business and Design: a preliminary assignment and SAT or ACT test results.</p></div>
            
  </div>

</div>
      </div>
  </div>

      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-accordion"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
  <div class="paragraph--text-accordion component-container">
      <div class="accordion__container">
                  <h2>  Admission round B
</h2>
                          <div class="listing-accordion__description">  <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>You can apply to the following bachelor's programmes in admission round B:</p>
<ul>
<li>Bachelor’s Programme in Design and Media&nbsp;</li>
<li>Bachelor’s Programme in Technology, Business, and Design</li>
<li>Bachelor’s Programme in Economics</li>
<li>Bachelor’s Programme in Finance</li>
<li>Bachelor's Programme in International Business</li>
</ul>
<p>Bachelor's Programme in Science and Technology, study options:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Chemical Engineering</li>
<li>Computer Engineering</li>
<li>Data Science</li>
<li>Digital Systems and Design</li>
<li>Mechanical and Civil Engineering</li>
<li>Quantum Technology</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Eligibility in admission round B: </strong>Applicants who have completed or will complete in spring 2027 the Finnish Matriculation Examination, the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/">International Baccalaureate (IB)</a>, the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.eursc.eu/en/European-Schools/European-Baccalaureate" title="European Baccalaureate">European Baccalaureate&nbsp;(EB)</a>, the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.dsh.fi/de/oberstufe/deutsches-internationales-abitur-dia/" title="Deutsches Internationales Abitur (DIA)">Deutsches Internationales Abitur (DIA)</a> / Reifeprüfung (RP) completed at Deutsche Schule Helsinki.</p>
<p><strong>Study option Bachelor’s Programme in Design and Media</strong>: Eligible to this study option in admission round B are also applicants who fulfill the general eligibility requirements for higher education. See the section <em>Who can apply.</em></p>
<p><strong>Admission result publication:</strong> The admission results for admission round B are published by 28 May 2027.&nbsp;</p></div>
</div>
                <div class="listing-accordion__container">  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--5"
          id="accordion-title--5"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Admission method in admission round B
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--5" id="accordion-content--5">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>In the fields of science and technology or business and economics the selection is based on the grades obtained in the Finnish Matriculation Examination, <a href="https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/">International Baccalaureate (IB)</a>, the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.eursc.eu/en/European-Schools/European-Baccalaureate" title="European Baccalaureate">European Baccalaureate&nbsp;(EB)</a>, the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.dsh.fi/de/oberstufe/deutsches-internationales-abitur-dia/" title="Deutsches Internationales Abitur (DIA)">Deutsches Internationales Abitur (DIA)</a> / Reifeprüfung (RP) completed at Deutsche Schule Helsinki.</p>
<p>For the Technology, Business and Design programme, admission is based on a preliminary assignment and on the grades obtained in the Finnish Matriculation Examination, International Baccalaureate (IB), the&nbsp;European Baccalaureate&nbsp;(EB), the&nbsp;Deutsches Internationales Abitur (DIA) / Reifeprüfung (RP) completed at Deutsche Schule Helsinki.</p>
<p>For the Design and Media programme, admission is based on&nbsp;preliminary assignments, intake assignments, and an interview.</p>
<p>For the Finance and International Business programmes, there is also an alternative admission method based on SAT or ACT test scores.<br>&nbsp;</p></div>
            
  </div>

</div>
      </div>
  </div>

      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-text"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
      <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text-text paragraph--view-mode--default">
      <div class="text-text">
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><h3><strong>Order of preference of study options</strong></h3>
<p>Rank your study options in the order of preference on the application form. Place highest the study option you are most interested in. Keep in mind that if you are admitted to your first or second preference option, your lower preferences will be automatically cancelled. You can change the study options or their order of preference only during the application period, from 7 to 22 January 2027.&nbsp;</p></div>
            </div>
    </div>
  
      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-accordion"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
  <div class="paragraph--text-accordion component-container">
      <div class="accordion__container">
                        <div class="listing-accordion__container">  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--6"
          id="accordion-title--6"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Application fee
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--6" id="accordion-content--6">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>Applicants who are not citizens of the European Union (EU), or the European Economic Area (EEA) member states, or Switzerland must pay a €100 application fee to apply for higher education in Finland.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Citizens of EU or EEA member states and Switzerland are exempt from the fee. In addition, certain types of Finnish residence permits provide an exemption from the fee. Detailed information on the application fee, exemptions and payment instructions are available on the Studyinfo page&nbsp;<a href="https://opintopolku.fi/konfo/en/sivu/application-fee">Application fee</a>.</p>
<p>If you have a document that exempts you from the application fee, you must upload it to your application form.</p>
<p>The application fee is collected by the Finnish National Agency for Education&nbsp;in connection with filling out the application form in the Studyinfo.fi service. Payment must be made within seven days of submitting your application. The fee cannot be paid late. Unpaid applications will not be processed.</p>
<p>The application fee is statutory and non-negotiable; no waivers are available.</p>
<p>Please note that paying the fee does not guarantee admission to university.&nbsp;</p>
<p>If you have questions about application fees after reviewing the&nbsp;<a href="https://opintopolku.fi/konfo/en/sivu/application-fee">Application fee</a> page, please contact the National Agency for Education at applicationfee@oph.fi.</p></div>
            
  </div>

  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--7"
          id="accordion-title--7"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Scholarships and tuition fees
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--7" id="accordion-content--7">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>Bachelor's and master's programmes have a tuition fee for students who are not citizens of the EU/EEA countries or Switzerland.&nbsp;Aalto University offers a very limited number of scholarships to outstanding applicants who are liable to tuition fees.&nbsp;</p>
<p>For details, see&nbsp;<a href="/en/node/30591">Scholarships and Tuition Fees</a>.&nbsp;</p></div>
            
  </div>

</div>
      </div>
  </div>

      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-accordion"
        lang="en"       style="">
    
  <div class="paragraph--text-accordion component-container">
      <div class="accordion__container">
                  <h2>  Admission results
</h2>
                          <div class="listing-accordion__description">  <div class="aalto-user-generated-content">
<p>The admission results for admission round A are published in the&nbsp;Studyinfo&nbsp;service by&nbsp;31 March 2027.</p>
<p>The admission results for admission round B are published in the&nbsp;Studyinfo&nbsp;service by&nbsp;28 May 2027</p>
</div>

</div>
                <div class="listing-accordion__container">  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--8"
          id="accordion-title--8"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Accepting your study place offer
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--8" id="accordion-content--8">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>If you have been admitted to a study programme, you will receive an email notification. You can only be admitted to your highest study option preference for which your admission results are sufficient. &nbsp;</p>
<p>When all the admission results have been published, you can be admitted off the waiting list. Please note that if all study places have been filled, no one will be admitted off the waiting list.&nbsp;Admission from the waiting list ends on 3 August 2027, or earlier if all study places are filled.</p>
<p>You must accept the offer of admission by the given deadline, otherwise the admission offer will be cancelled.&nbsp;The offer acceptance is binding. Once you have accepted the offer, the acceptance cannot be cancelled. When you bindingly accept the admission offer, your applications to other study options will be cancelled automatically.</p>
<p>View more information about accepting your study place and other information for newly admitted students on the&nbsp;<a href="/en/node/738111">new bachelor’s students</a> page. The page will be updated in spring 2027.</p>
<p>Important information about accepting your study place offer and enrolment can be found at&nbsp;<a href="https://opintopolku.fi/konfo/en/sivu/how-to-accept-an-offer-of-admission-in-joint-application-to-higher-education">Studyinfo</a>.</p></div>
            
  </div>

  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--9"
          id="accordion-title--9"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    You can accept only one study place leading to a higher education degree in Finland
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--9" id="accordion-content--9">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>You can only accept one study place leading to a higher education degree in Finland for education that begins in the same academic term.&nbsp;<a href="https://opintopolku.fi/konfo/en/sivu/provisions-and-restrictions-regarding-student-admissions-to-higher-education#one-study-place-per-term-provision">The one study place per term provision</a>&nbsp;applies to all higher education&nbsp;in universities and universities of applied sciences in Finland.&nbsp;</p>
<p>If you applied to multiple study options or in different application rounds, it is likely that you will not receive the admission results for all of your study option preferences at the same time. Think carefully whether you wish to accept an offered study place or wait for the results of your other study options.</p></div>
            
  </div>

  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--10"
          id="accordion-title--10"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Submitting a rectification request
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--10" id="accordion-content--10">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>The rectification request procedure gives you the possibility to appeal your admission results if you believe that there has been an error in the admission decision-making process. The rectification request must be submitted to the University Registry within 14 days of the publication of the admission results. The University will not process rectification requests received after the deadline or before the publication of the results. Rectification request must contain the grounds for your request. Rectification requests are not intended to be used as a tool for requesting feedback or additional information on the admission process, including admission results.</p>
<p>For details, see&nbsp;<a href="/en/node/635871">instructions for requesting rectification to student admissions</a>.</p></div>
            
  </div>

</div>
      </div>
  </div>

      </div>

                
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--single-liftup-medium"
        lang="en"       style="">
